    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0281" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg149"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/7–745:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 129 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Murphy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hoechst</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-07T14:00:00+03:00">July 7, 1945—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. Your 61, July 5, 11 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d129-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I thank you for your invitation to attend the meeting of the three heads of
                    govt.</p>
                <p>
                    General Clay and I are proceeding to
                    Berlin this morning and we shall do everything possible to ensure that
                    satisfactory arrangements are made in Berlin for the Dept’s delegation. I shall hope to telegraph you an account of the
                    situation tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Murphy</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
